competitive play for blizzards popular  first-person shooter overwatch has made  its way to Xbox one and it sounds like  it came a little bit early Blizzard  released an update from Microsoft's  console earlier today even though it  wasn't expected to arrive until next  week this update hasn't made its way to  ps4 yet but we'll be sure to let you  know once it does overwatch is  competitive play mode is available after  you reach level 25 once you do that it  will show up under the play button in  the main menu if you're unsure how  competitive play works head on over to  gamespot com for a detailed breakdown on  the mode this update also adds a number  of gameplay tweaks including an option  to adjust aim assist strength don't  worry though because the default aim  assist is already at full strength this  update also removes the avoid player  option in McCree is now available as an  AI hero in player verse AI and custom  matches speaking of McCree he got nerfed  his bullet damage has been decreased  additionally Widowmaker also took a  slight hit her head shots are still  deadly but body shots aren't quite as  powerful for a full list of changes and  more on overwatch check out our article  on gamespot com
 

